
=== Rest

Send changes from your relational database to a Rest endpoint in XML or JSON format.  A Rest node can be setup as a <<Write-Only Node>> to receive changes from another node that is capturing changes.

ifdef::pro[]
Set up the Rest node by using the Configure Diagram and selecting Rest as the type.   The URL will be the connection point to the Rest endpoint.

image::images/appendix/rest-node-setup.png[]

Further settings can be configured in the deploy wizard.

image::images/appendix/rest-advanced-settings.png[]
endif::pro[]

==== API Key

.Define an API key with the following property.
----
rest.writer.api.key
----
==== Output Message Format

.Set the output message format with the following property
----
rest.writer.format=JSON|XML
----

[horizontal]        
JSON::  Json formatted output message 
[source, json]
----
[
  {
    "table name": {
      "eventType": "INSERT|UPDATE|DELETE",
      "data": {
        "column name": "value",....
      }
    }
  }
]    
----
[horizontal]
XML::  Xml formatted output message
[source, xml]
----
<rows>
	<row entity="table name" dml="INSERT|UPDATE|DELETE">
		<data key="column name">value</data>
		...
	</row>
</rows>
----


